          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "One or more servers may respond with DHCPOFFER messages containing a proposed address, lease time, and configuration options. The client chooses an offer and broadcasts DHCPREQUEST identifying the selected server and address. Broadcasting the choice informs the winning server to proceed and allows other servers to withdraw their pending offers. This is a coordination step, not merely a repeat of the request. Packet captures reveal the selected-server and requested-address options that make the client's intent explicit."
