        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "Troubleshooting follows the exchange. Confirm link and VLAN first. Capture whether Discover leaves the client, whether the relay forwards it, whether an Offer returns, and whether Request and Acknowledgment complete. Then inspect the scope for exhaustion, option errors, reservations, and lease conflicts. Also ask who is answering: a rogue DHCP server can supply a malicious gateway or DNS setting. DORA is therefore both an availability workflow and a trust boundary. Seeing each packet in context turns 'the network is down' into a testable sequence of hypotheses."
        },
        "model": "edge-tts-7.2.8",
